## Provenance

The behavioural requirements in `docs/` were reconstructed from 426 screenshots of a
production system plus four import templates and two report exports. That product is
referred to throughout as *the observed product*.

No vendor source code, build artefacts, proprietary assets, logos or branding are
included. Reconstructed screen inventories, field names and ledger codes are recorded
as **evidence**, not as reusable assets. AIMSCAMS is an independent implementation and
is not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by, or certified by the observed
product's vendor.

The reference tenant used to validate the reconstruction is **Mafanikio Financial
Services Limited (MFSL)**, a microfinance institution in Tanzania. Its name appears
because it was the tenant under observation; it does not imply a commercial
relationship, endorsement, or authorisation beyond that observation.

## Personal data

The screenshot corpus contains personal data of real individuals (names, telephone
numbers, national identification fragments). It is deliberately **not** committed to
this repository. See `README.md#evidence-and-privacy` and the Tanzanian Personal Data
Protection Act 2022.

Any tenant data introduced during pilot or migration must be handled under a written
data-processing agreement and must never be committed to this repository.

